# Spec Chum — agent rules map

## Precedence

1. User instructions
2. Cross-tool project constraints in `AGENTS.md`
3. This map and tool-specific `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (workflow detail; cannot override 1 or 2)
4. `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `docs/*` for contributor and topic detail

## Hard constraints (never violate)

- No plan edits under `.cursor/plans/`
- No ROM binaries in git (`./scripts/fetch_roms.sh`)
- No macOS **system** speaker volume changes
- Prefer additive, owning-crate changes; no drive-by cross-crate refactors
- Release tag `vX.Y.Z` requires `./scripts/run_slow_tests.sh` (default CI ≠ enough)

## Rules index (open for detail)

| Concern | Open |
| --- | --- |
| Merge / CodeRabbit gate | `pr-review-merge.mdc` → detail in `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Bot finding disposition + code habits | `coderabbit-lessons.mdc` |
| GUI host parity (4 hosts, same PR) | `gui-app-parity.mdc` |
| Architecture exploration / graphify | `graphify.mdc` |
| GitHub Issues sync | `github-issues.mdc` |
| Tools vs Shell | `prefer-tools-over-cli.mdc` |
| Rust idioms (glob `*.rs`) | `rust.mdc` |
| Crate map / workflow / cloud | `AGENTS.md` |

## Always-on checklist

1. Follow `AGENTS.md` → “Agentic coding loop” for scope, progress notes, handoffs, and human decision points.
2. Check related issues for substantive implementation → `github-issues.mdc`
3. Use graphify when architectural context or call paths are unclear → `graphify.mdc`
4. GUI change? Update **all** first-party hosts in **same PR** → `gui-app-parity.mdc`
5. Feature work? Prefer behavior-complete vertical slices; use horizontal work for layer-wide or accuracy-driven changes → `AGENTS.md`
6. Match checks to scope; use `./scripts/check_crates.sh` while iterating and `./scripts/check.sh` for full-workspace/merge readiness · Living room: `./scripts/check_living_room.sh` (release)
7. Finish/merge PR? Follow `pr-review-merge.mdc` (**CI soft-pass ≠ merge-ready**)

## Emulator crates (core)

`z80`, `bus`, `ula`, `tape`, `formats`, `machine`, `app` (+ hosts: SpecChumMac, `windows_shell`, `linux_shell`).
